[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843091397","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105962#issuecomment-2843091397","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105962","id":2843091397,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pdiHF","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-30T19:40:55Z","updated_at":"2025-04-30T19:40:55Z","body":"Hmm, not sure why it started failing all of the sudden; maybe the explicit use of `NeverNull` threw something off? Gonna mark as a draft while I figure this out\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2843091397/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845288772","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105962#issuecomment-2845288772","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105962","id":2845288772,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pl6lE","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T17:14:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T17:19:54Z","body":"Cool to see more people tackling this, thanks a lot! :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\nIt seems the main difference of `NotNull` vs. `RequiredPtr` is that this one moves the validation to the call site, thus causing an error earlier?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nWhat's very elegant in @dsnopek's PR #86079 is that it's statically impossible to obtain the inner pointer when the value is null (type-state pattern). This provides the confidence that the precondition of a function is truly upheld.\r\n\r\nIn this PR on the other hand, we have\r\n```rs\r\n\r\nvoid Node::add_child(NotNull<Node *> p_child, bool p_force_readable_name, InternalMode p_internal) {\r\n\tERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(data.inside_tree && !Thread::is_main_thread(), \"Adding children to a node inside the SceneTree is only allowed from the main thread. Use call_deferred(\\\"add_child\\\",node).\");\r\n\r\n\tERR_THREAD_GUARD\r\n\tERR_FAIL_NULL(p_child);\r\n\r\n\t... // actual function logic\r\n}\r\n```\r\nand it's possible to accidentally forget the `ERR_FAIL_NULL` check, thus running into follow-up logic errors or even undefined behavior.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> An alternative to David's `RequiredPtr`, implemented as a generic wrapper instead.\r\n\r\nOne thing that cannot be done inside a template like `NonNull` is a descriptive error message: you will get something generic like \"non-null value assigned null\", rather than \"non-null parameter 'p_child' is null\".\r\n\r\n`RequiredPtr` also seems quite a bit simpler, without massive SFINAE machinery?\r\n\r\nWhere do you see the main advantages of this approach vs. `RequiredPtr`? Maybe it's somehow possible to combine the benefits of both? :thinking: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845288772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845341025","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105962#issuecomment-2845341025","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105962","id":2845341025,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pmHVh","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T17:42:05Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T17:42:05Z","body":"The most obvious benefit is when using `NeverNull<T>`, this check wouldn't be necessary. This would, however, change internal behavior such that Godot **would** crash if passed a non-null pointer, which seems counter to Godot's goals. However, in many cases, those kinds of errors aren't recoverable in the first place, so maybe that's what we should be doing regardless? If we did that, it would effectively remove the SFINAE hurdles entirely, but would be compatibility-breaking\r\n\r\nI'll whip up an alternative PR to give that style a spin, see which we wanna roll with","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845341025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845365054","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105962#issuecomment-2845365054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105962","id":2845365054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pmNM-","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-01T17:55:33Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T17:55:33Z","body":"> However, in many cases, those kinds of errors aren't recoverable in the first place\r\n\r\nBut they are recoverable as of today, no? Even if \"print error and return\" isn't necessarily the best course of action, it's in line with Godot's [no-crash philosophy](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/about/faq.html#why-does-godot-not-use-exceptions) as you say :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> The most obvious benefit is when using `NeverNull<T>`, this check wouldn't be necessary.\r\n\r\nBut in all other cases (likely the majority), the `RequiredPtr` pattern would still be safer to use and provide more precise error messages.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2845365054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3702185902","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105962#issuecomment-3702185902","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105962","id":3702185902,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cqt-u","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-31T13:10:37Z","updated_at":"2025-12-31T13:13:18Z","body":"With https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/2241 now implemented, is this still relevant? :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\nSame question for\r\n- #106756\r\n- #90767\r\n- #106847\r\n- #106418","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3702185902/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3778548561","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105962#issuecomment-3778548561","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105962","id":3778548561,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hOBNR","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T14:53:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T14:53:06Z","body":"I think this concept still has merit, but it needs to be re-evaluated in the context of #86079 being merged. Same goes for the other listed PRs.\r\n\r\nClosing for now, will likely revisit at a later date","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3778548561/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]